=== LITEM Shadow00
Black Witch claw
The only physical part of shadow. Used in magical rituals.

=== LITEM Shadow00_2
Black sorcerer claw
They say when restless souls leave killed shadows, they settle in these claws. Magicians will always buy them.

=== LITEM Shadow00_3
Black seer claw
A necessary element of magical rituals for casting certain spells.

=== LITEM Shadow00_4
Black magician claw
They say it is used for casting the most powerful spells...

=== LITEM SpiderSting
Sting of young spider
In crushed form they are used to make drugs and paints.

=== LITEM SpiderSting_2
Sting of spider
They are cheap but are widely used, so they are always in demand.

=== LITEM SpiderSting_3
Sting of large spider
Crushed spider stings are popular among ageing noblemen - apparently they bring back youth.

=== LITEM SuccubusGreen00
Head of young harpy
A scarecrow like that set in front of the gates would keep more than just thieves away.

=== LITEM SuccubusGreen00_2
Head of harpy
This head on a spike in front of the gates would serve as a fair warning to criminals.

=== LITEM SuccubusGreen00_3
Head of adult harpy
It can be bought for a practical joke. It would be an expensive one, though.

=== LITEM SuccubusGreen00_4
Head of old harpy
Many a collector is combing the markets for a trophy like that.

=== LITEM SuccubusRed00
Head of young red harpy
A head like that on a spike in front of the village gates would keep other Harpies away.

=== LITEM SuccubusRed00_2
Head of red harpy
Brigands would never venture into a village if they saw a head like this on a spike, right in front of the gates...

=== LITEM SuccubusRed00_3
Head of adult red harpy
If you see this on a spike in front of the gates, you know not to quarrel with the locals.

=== LITEM ToadLegs00
Small Toad legs
Toads may spit poison but their meat is quite edible, so there is always a demand for it.

=== LITEM ToadLegs00_2
Toad legs
They pay good money for these: a nice addition to the family table.

=== LITEM ToadLegs00_3
Fat Toad legs
Legs of grown Toads are tender, considered a delicacy and cost good money.

=== LITEM UnicornHorn00
Horn of young Black Unicorn
It is widely believed that unicorn's horn is a poison indicator, so there is always demand for them.

=== LITEM UnicornHorn00_2
Horn of Black Unicorn
A very rare thing, and a good antidote too.

=== LITEM UnicornHorn00_3
Large horn of  Black Unicorn
These are always in demand!

=== LITEM UnicornHorn01
Horn of young White Unicorn
This is the best poison indicator, so it is always in demand.

=== LITEM UnicornHorn01_2
Horn of White Unicorn
There'll be no problem selling such a prize!

=== LITEM UnicornHorn01_3
Large horn of White Unicorn
The most noble and rich consider it stylish to serve wine in these.

=== LITEM WhiteTigerSkin
Young White Tiger skin
An excellent decoration for homes, and costs a lot.

=== LITEM WhiteTigerSkin_2
White Tiger skin
Highly valuable, especially where there are no Tigers.

=== LITEM WhiteTigerSkin_3
Old White Tiger skin
A rich man will pay a lot to be able to boast how he killed that Tiger...

=== LITEM WhiteWolfSkin
Young White Wolf fangs
Even a young White Wolf makes a more honourable trophy than an adult grey one.

=== LITEM WhiteWolfSkin_2
White wolf fangs
A necklace made of these will be more expensive than one made of common wolves' fangs.

=== LITEM WhiteWolfSkin_3
Large White Wolf fangs
The most expensive decorations are made of these.

